# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
import { defineComponent, type PropType } from "vue";

export default defineComponent({
  props: {
    a: [String, Boolean],
    b: { type: [String, Boolean] as PropType<string | boolean> },
  },
});

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-define-component.ts:6:17 lint/nursery/useVueBooleanPropTypeFirst  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! Boolean isn't the first type of this prop.
  
    4 │ export default defineComponent({
    5 │   props: {
  > 6 │     a: [String, Boolean],
      │                 ^^^^^^^
    7 │     b: { type: [String, Boolean] as PropType<string | boolean> },
    8 │   },
  
  i When String comes before Boolean, a prop written in a template without a value, such as <MyComponent disabled />, is set to an empty string instead of true.
  
  i Move Boolean to the start of the list of types.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Move Boolean to the start of the list.
  
